{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334551-blowing-holes-in-the-gauntlet","id":1334551,"title":"Blowing holes in the Gauntlet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-08T16:34:19-07:00","id":1334551,"title":"Blowing holes in the Gauntlet","content":"So...any rat shard who just occupied a human being can start gnawing at the gauntlet and either lower the level, or even remove it outright in certain areas causing holes in the gauntlet. Other entities can do this too, such as the Shadow Gate Manifestation, or the power of the Idigam to manipulate gauntlet. There are many creatures that can lower the gauntlet, or even cause a hole where there is no gauntlet.<br /> <br /> From a storytelling point of view, what happens after that? Do spirits start flooding out or does it take them time to notice and start using it. Once the gauntlet has been breached do the spirit courts announce &quot;RUN TO THE FLESH BEFORE THE URATHA COME!&quot; and start a stampede towards the exits, or can a gauntlet breach exist for a while before it leaks anything. When the spirits do start using it do they consider coming back to the Hisil or are they hoping it is a one way ticket? I would imagine if a good chunk of spirits came out of a gap, such that there are dozens of claimed or spirits in the area, it would probably take the local forsaken pack months if not years to clean up the mess. Is it like a &quot;prison break&quot; episode where a rat opens the initial breach and other spirits open the breach further to free their kindred spirits (&quot;you are free comrades!&quot;)? How long would it take for the Forsaken to notice? I would imagine that a pack of Hunters in Darkness who's territory is a city block will notice much faster than a territory the size of half a rural county run by Blood Talons who are mostly focused on the Pure. How much havoc could a spirit, or Idigam, do when she uses her gauntlet manipulating powers to blow, say, 5 or 10 holes in a short time just to see the mayhem it would cause. And... let's not forget a master Mage who wants to open a really BIG hole in the gauntlet because he is power hungry and, maybe a little nuts.<br /> <br /> In addition, how would this be different if it occured in Pure territory? Say a rat host opens a hole and gets a flood of spirits out, just to be greeted by a pack of Fire Touched. Would the Pure smile and say &quot;Hey, lets make this hole even bigger!&quot; If the Fire Touched are fond of letting spirits run free in the flesh, who is to say that any Fire touched territory is a potential, massive, gauntlet breach waiting to happen. By that point, it would probably be best for the Forsaken to just invade the place, though it would be quite a mess to deal with afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T19:12:46-07:00","id":1334568,"title":"","content":"You're looking for generalities when such scenarios should fit the terms of your story. If you need spirits pouring into the Flesh like it's open season, they do that. If the spirit courts are smart enough to keep the backdoor hidden, they do that instead. And no: Claiming requires the Control influence, as such, only rank 3 spirits and above may attempt to claim a mount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T20:41:27-07:00","id":1334573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334551-blowing-holes-in-the-gauntlet#post1334551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a storytelling point of view, what happens after that? Do spirits start flooding out or does it take them time to notice and start using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits don't general have a concrete sense for the state of the Gauntlet outside of their immediate presence unless that's something they can specifically do as an individual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once the gauntlet has been breached do the spirit courts announce &quot;RUN TO THE FLESH BEFORE THE URATHA COME!&quot; and start a stampede towards the exits, or can a gauntlet breach exist for a while before it leaks anything. </div> </div> </div>This will depend heavily upon how congested and how lucid the local Shadow is. Is there a large number of intelligent spirits struggling among themselves for control of the territory and/or survival? Some of them will probably seize the opportunity if they come across a hole in the veil. Is it mostly a quiet zone occupied by spirits young enough to still correspond to singular phenomena? They're probably not going to go out of their way to look unless they're the sort of things that like to wriggle in between the cracks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the spirits do start using it do they consider coming back to the Hisil or are they hoping it is a one way ticket? </div> </div> </div>Most spirits who leave the Shadow are going to be middling in Rank and looking for breathing room and reduced competition over easier food. The stronger ones may have a specific agenda they aim to carry out that requires some form of free passage to be sorted out, and if that's the case then they may very well look to Claim a mount to make the passing easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334551-blowing-holes-in-the-gauntlet?p=1334568#post1334568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no: Claiming requires the Control influence, as such, only rank 3 spirits and above may attempt to claim a mount.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least, that's the case outside of very specialized circumstances; one look at the Devourer Hound writeup will show you Gafflings aren't locked out of the <i>duguthim</i> game.<br /> <br /> (Also, Claiming itself just requires the Controlled Condition, which is achievable with time and repeated Possession.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T05:27:35-07:00","id":1334616,"title":"","content":"The issue with spirits making <i>duguthim </i>is that they need so many manifestations to even survive/be effective that's pretty fucking specialized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T06:21:49-07:00","id":1334626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334551-blowing-holes-in-the-gauntlet?p=1334616#post1334616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with spirits making <i>duguthim </i>is that they need so many manifestations to even survive/be effective that's pretty fucking specialized.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between &quot;A Rank 3+ spirit doesn't have to spend Numina slots getting enough extra Manifestations to qualify for this and has the capacity to kick this process off without taking several scenes of prep&quot; and &quot;Spirits require Rank 3+ to do this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T09:52:19-07:00","id":1334665,"title":"","content":"By the time they have enough manifestation for that, they're probably rank 3 anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T13:14:25-07:00","id":1334708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334551-blowing-holes-in-the-gauntlet#post1334551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a storytelling point of view, what happens after that? Do spirits start flooding out or does it take them time to notice and start using it. Once the gauntlet has been breached do the spirit courts announce &quot;RUN TO THE FLESH BEFORE THE URATHA COME!&quot; and start a stampede towards the exits, or can a gauntlet breach exist for a while before it leaks anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever seen the Wire? The Hamsterdam arc? Or the Purge? Not every spirit is just a rampant barbarian eager to break the rules of their life and jump into the gurihal, but some might be pushed to it, as victims of excessive predation, starvation, or the oppressive gravity of Helios. Most powerful or established spirits could probably cross the Gauntlet without outside help, but don't because they've managed to find a way to thrive there. Also, remember, Father Wolf was the God of the Border Marches, werewolves are limited to both sides of the Gauntlet. Between this, and being superb trackers, just getting to a gauntlet breach fast doesn't mean you'll be in the clear. It's the thing most likely to gain Uratha attention, which can lead to hunts, and death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the spirits do start using it do they consider coming back to the Hisil or are they hoping it is a one way ticket? I would imagine if a good chunk of spirits came out of a gap, such that there are dozens of claimed or spirits in the area, it would probably take the local forsaken pack months if not years to clean up the mess. Is it like a &quot;prison break&quot; episode where a rat opens the initial breach and other spirits open the breach further to free their kindred spirits (&quot;you are free comrades!&quot;)? </div> </div> </div>Since you're escaping to the gurihal because you need to, going back wouldn't really be a high priority unless things had changed drastically on that side, or if said spirit crossing to do something was part of a larger plan. Either way as noted above it's pretty much all storyteller fiat.<br /> <br /> That said, dozens of claimed or spirits, especially new ones, can be cleared out pretty quickly by a pack who's intent on it. Between abilities to locate spirits in their territories, their own tracking abilities, alarms to detect Claimed, they're well prepared for this kind of situation, and it would be smarter to cut off any Claimed before they get established.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How long would it take for the Forsaken to notice? I would imagine that a pack of Hunters in Darkness who's territory is a city block will notice much faster than a territory the size of half a rural county run by Blood Talons who are mostly focused on the Pure. How much havoc could a spirit, or Idigam, do when she uses her gauntlet manipulating powers to blow, say, 5 or 10 holes in a short time just to see the mayhem it would cause. And... let's not forget a master Mage who wants to open a really BIG hole in the gauntlet because he is power hungry and, maybe a little nuts. </div> </div> </div>Between Luna's prophetic dreams and things like Read the World's Loom, as well as the assorted alliances werewolves can have with spriits, it's possible they would know about it before it even happened. There are also a lot of territory-wide abilities that would help them find out fast, providing you had a pack that had an emphasis on paying attention to the Hisil.<br /> <br /> It's the type of thing that can be disastrous for humans, or werewolves who for whatever reason don't put much focus on the spirit world, maybe being new, or all focused on the flesh. But if it happened in your territory, you have a wide variety of tools at your disposal to not only be aware of things like this, but to quickly shut them down.<br /> <br /> Even with a prepared pack things can go bad, if for some reason there's a powerful spirit that's unleashed, maybe even some ancient powerful beshilu shard or other thing stuck in the Gauntlet. But 'a lot of smaller things, in your territory' is much easier to deal with. The more powerful, and farther from your territory it is, the worse the fallout can be. It's not as if beshilu are mindless, either, they'd likely recruit spirits of rats and disease. You can see in the fiction for the core book what happens in the lead-up to a beshilu 'victory.' But if this happens in a neighboring territory, perhaps by werewolves (or other supernaturals) who aren't interested in anything but keeping other werewolves out, you have chances of things getting a lot worse, especially since said supernaturals could be the victims of Claiming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, how would this be different if it occured in Pure territory? Say a rat host opens a hole and gets a flood of spirits out, just to be greeted by a pack of Fire Touched. Would the Pure smile and say &quot;Hey, lets make this hole even bigger!&quot; If the Fire Touched are fond of letting spirits run free in the flesh, who is to say that any Fire touched territory is a potential, massive, gauntlet breach waiting to happen. By that point, it would probably be best for the Forsaken to just invade the place, though it would be quite a mess to deal with afterwards. </div> </div> </div>Fire-Touched would be the bigger issue, not all Pure are intent on letting the world burn, but Fire-Touched eager to do this would likely attempt to make sure neighboring Forsaken that could stop them would be eliminated beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T14:41:59-07:00","id":1334712,"title":"","content":"The Fire-Touched are an interesting case in this scenario. They\u2019re generally very pro-spirit, but their Sacred Hunt is literally those who dishonor and disrespect the Shadow. Note this isn\u2019t those who dishonor spirits, it\u2019s the Shadow. If a Gauntlet breach occurred and a bunch of spirits flooded across because \u2018screw that place, the flesh has got to be better\u2019, they\u2019re going to find out very quickly the nuance between what they think the Fire-Touched stand for, and what the Fire-Touched actually stand for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T19:57:30-07:00","id":1334755,"title":"","content":"that is an interesting take and one I support. But I do want to know. is that canon or your (pretty cool) headcanon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T01:27:53-07:00","id":1334777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334551-blowing-holes-in-the-gauntlet?p=1334755#post1334755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that is an interesting take and one I support. But I do want to know. is that canon or your (pretty cool) headcanon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T06:42:33-07:00","id":1334842,"title":"","content":"The part about the fire-Touched hunting Spirits who disrespect the Shadow by their actions too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T05:48:58-07:00","id":1335095,"title":"","content":"Fire-Touched Sacred Hunt being those who disrespect the Shadow is canon. Like all Pure, individual Fire-Touched generally get to determine where the line is for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T09:56:05-07:00","id":1337333,"title":"","content":"I like Claimed and don't particularly care about the systems as much as having them in the Game. Sure, rank 2 spirits can become Claimed in my games. If you think it's cool then go for it, don't be held back by mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T12:39:04-07:00","id":1337672,"title":"","content":"Dragon Age Inquisition all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}